# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# The harness runs the image CMD so services actually boot. The CMD points at
# entrypoint.ps1, which is PID-1-safe:
#   * sshd + WinRM are started first;
#   * Elasticsearch (elasticsearch.bat) is launched in the BACKGROUND via
#     Start-Process, so the JVM is a detached child, NOT PID 1;
#   * PID 1 is an idle `while ($true) { Start-Sleep -Seconds 60 }` loop.
#
# ES has no runtime reload for node-level scripting settings, so the honest fix
# REQUIRES restarting ES. That is safe now - the ES JVM is not PID 1, so stopping
# and relaunching it never kills the container. Heap is capped (ES_HEAP_SIZE=512m)
# to avoid OOMing the VM.
